By Brokard wrt.  $(NKLM)$ , we know that  $ML\cap NK$  lies on the polar of  $H=MK\cap NL$ , so it suffices to show that  $AB$  is the polar of  $H$ . Because  $CD\perp AB$ , this is equivalent to showing that  $H$  and  $D$  are inverses. However because  $EHDA$  is cyclic,  $CH\cdot CD=CE\cdot CA=r^2$  where  $r$  is the radius of  $(NKLM)$ .

