Let  $S=EF\cap BC$ . Let  $G$  be the Miquel point of  $FECB$ . By standard Miquel stuff, we see that  $G$  is the inverse of  $H$  about  $(BFEC)$ , and by Brokard on  $FECB$ ,  $G$  then lies on  $AS$  with  $MG\perp AS$ .

<u>Claim:</u>  $SP$  is tangent to  $\omega$ .
<u>Proof of Claim:</u> Let  $\Phi_A$  inversion about  $\omega$ . Since  $\omega$  has radius  $\sqrt{AH\cdot AD}=\sqrt{AF\cdot AB}=\sqrt{AR\cdot AC}$ , we see that  $\Phi_A F=B$ ,  $\Phi_A H=D$ , and  $\Phi_A E=C$ . Therefore,  $\Phi_A S=\Phi_A(EF\cap BC)=(ABC)\cap(AEF)=G$ . Note that  $(AGP)$  is tangent to  $\omega$  since the center of  $(AGP)$  is the midpoint of  $AP$ . Thus, since  $\Phi_A((AGP))=SP$ , and  $\Phi_A(\omega)=\omega$ , we see that  $SP$  is tangent to  $\omega$  (inversion preserves tangencies).  $\blacksquare$ Thus, we see that  $SP^2=SA\cdot SG$  (since  $SP$  is also tangent to  $(AGP)$ ), and  $SA\cdot SG=SB\cdot SC$ , so  $SP^2=SB\cdot SC$ , which implies that  $SP$  is also tangent to  $(PBC)$ . This completes the proof since we have shown that  $SP$  is tangent to both  $\omega$  and  $(PBC)$  at  $P$ .

Q.E.D.

P.S. You might notice that  $\omega$ ,  $EF$  and  $(ABC)$  concur. We can show this by inversion. We see that  $\Phi_A(EF\cap(ABC))=(ABC)\cap EF$ , so  $(ABC)\cap EF$  inverts to itself, or  $(ABC)\cap EF\in\omega$ . In the second diagram with more points, there are also a few nontrivial concurrences, and those can also be proved in a similar fashion with the appropriate inversions.


