Note that we have,
\begin{align*}
zw = (z + w)w + (z + w)z
\end{align*}
which yields,
\begin{align*}
z^2 + zw + w^2 = 0.
\end{align*}
From here it is clear that  $z$  and  $w$  are simply rotations of each other by a third root of unity. Thus the area of the equilateral triangle formed by  $z$ ,  $z\omega$  and  $z\omega^2$  is simply,
\begin{align*}
\frac{3}{2} 2014^2 \sin 120^{\circ} = 3042\boxed{147} \sqrt{3}.
\end{align*}

